# Proactive model-recommendation callout (always)

Mirrors the owner's machine-global rule (`~/.cursor/rules/proactive-model-recommendation.mdc`),
duplicated here so a fresh clone on another machine still gets it even if the
global rules haven't been synced yet.

## When
At the start of every response that begins a new todo / feature / bug fix /
material refactor, or when the task type shifts (planning -> mechanical, code -> design, etc.).
Skip only for pure conversational replies with no new work.

## Format (keep <= 10 lines)
```
> **Model check.** Currently on `<current-model>`.
>
> **Best for this task:** `<best-outcome-model>` — <one line why>.
> - Pros: <one line>
> - Cons: <one line>
>
> **Budget alternative:** `<cheaper-or-faster-model>`.
> - Pros: <one line>
> - Cons: <one line>
>
> **My recommendation:** `<switch to X | stay on current>`.
> Reason: `<one line>`.
```

## Priority
Best outcome first; budget only when the user has explicitly asked for budget-first,
or the task is genuinely trivial (one-line fix, rename, mechanical find/replace).

## Model slugs commonly used
- Opus (4.7 / 4.8 / 5): deep planning, design taste, debugging, long-form.
- Sonnet (4.6 / 5.5): everyday features, refactors across files, docs.
- GPT-5.3 Codex: pure code refactor, escape Claude loops.
- Composer / Gemini Flash: tiny targeted edits, batch, image understanding.

Users always decide — the callout is guidance.
